{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6j8xwV2QWPCYv7tB2Fj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class, and define `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values. When an Order is created, it defaults to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Add new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that takes an orderId path variable\n   - Returns the Order on success (200)\n   - Validates the order exists (404 if not)\n   - Checks all shipments of that order: if ANY is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409) and make no changes\n   - Otherwise, update order status to CANCELLED and update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - If order already CANCELLED, succeed and change nothing (idempotent)\n\n3. **ShipmentController.kt**: Modify the `create` endpoint to check if the order being shipped is CANCELLED, and if so, reject with ConflictException (409). This validation happens before checking if shipment ID already exists.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt**: Add new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (for when cancel fails due to confirmed shipment)\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for when trying to create shipment for cancelled order)\n\n5. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order succeeds and returns CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling a CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order fails with 404\n   - CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n\n6. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test that creating shipment for CANCELLED order fails with 409\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n\n- **Service layer vs. controller business logic**: The requirement preserves existing architecture (no service layer currently), so logic goes in controllers. Adding a service layer would be architectural change outside scope.\n\n- **New OrderStatus enum vs. String status**: Using an enum (like ShipmentStatus) is consistent with existing patterns and provides type safety.\n\n- **Storing shipment references in Order vs. querying from repository**: The controller can query ShipmentRepository by orderId. This keeps Order immutable and simple.\n\n- **Optimistic locking vs. simple state checks**: For this simple in-memory store with single-threaded tests, state checks are sufficient.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order with no CONFIRMED shipments**:\n   - Input: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Check: Order exists → 404 if not\n   - Check: No shipment is CONFIRMED → if any is, throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT) with 409\n   - Action: Update Order.status to CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Output: 200 OK with updated Order\n\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED order**:\n   - Input: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Check: Order exists → 404 if not\n   - Check: Already cancelled, but continue anyway (idempotent)\n   - Check: No CONFIRMED shipments (will be none since order already cancelled)\n   - Action: Update Order to CANCELLED (no change)\n   - Output: 200 OK with Order\n\n3. **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment**:\n   - Input: POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Check: Order exists → 404 if not\n   - Check: CONFIRMED shipment exists → throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT) with 409\n   - Action: NONE - order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n   - Output: 409 with error envelope\n\n4. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order**:\n   - Input: POST /shipments with orderId pointing to CANCELLED order\n   - Check: Shipment ID doesn't already exist\n   - Check: Order exists\n   - Check: Order.status != CANCELLED → if cancelled, throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) with 409\n   - Action: NONE\n   - Output: 409 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n- `test_cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_returns_cancelled_status`: Create order, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED\n- `test_cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds`: Create order, cancel twice, verify second cancel succeeds\n- `test_cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_fails_with_409`: Create order, create shipment, confirm it (via direct repository), try cancel, verify 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n- `test_cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404`: Cancel non-existent order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- `test_cancel_cascades_created_shipments`: Create order, create multiple shipments, cancel order, verify all are CANCELLED\n- `test_cancelled_order_in_get_response`: Create and cancel order, GET it, verify status in response\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n- `test_create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_fails_with_409`: Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nI'll now implement the changes. Let me start by modifying the necessary files:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1455,"cache_read_input_tokens":24229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1455},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8eca444b-60ac-44f5-8846-36885f043d5b","uuid":"1ff7793c-b569-4266-9fab-64f70e3600ce","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:31:15.484Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6j8xVSfHjEqPGwhHeKS"}
